# Proposed features recognized from step_hole.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.
# imported with --up z- (model z- is machine +Z) -- coordinates are post-rotation

# F5: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F5_Top Plane(z=0.0)

# F6: outer profile under top cap F5: vertical wall loop F1 F4 F6 F2, top at z=0.0, base at z=-6.0, material inside the loop; stepped base: the profile stops at the highest base z=-6.0, and F1 to z=-10.0, F2 to z=-10.0, F4 to z=-10.0 run on below it; the base at z=-6.0 is the head's own underside (the face under the walls faces down): the wall is traced from above, the underside is the other setup's (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F6_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the base is stepped: this profile stops at z=-6.0, the highest base; the walls F1 F2 F4 run on below it
# and belong to whatever stands lower -- declare that by hand or accept its own proposal
# the base at z=-6.0 is an overhang: the face under the walls faces down, so the
# tool has air under it at the base; the underside itself is the other setup's
feature F6_Profile ProfileBoss(z=0.0, extent=6.0
    0.0 -40.0
    0.0 0.0
    60.0 0.0
    60.0 -40.0
)

# F10: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole, breaking out across 4 faces (F8, F3, F9, F7) (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F10_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=10.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F10_Hole, stepover=...)
feature F10_Hole CylinderBore(dia=8.0, extent=10.0, x=30.0, y=-12.0)

# F12: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F12_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=6.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F12_Hole, stepover=...)
feature F12_Hole CylinderBore(dia=6.0, extent=6.0, x=15.0, y=-28.0)
